---
description: When to use MongoDB vs Postgres in Astraq
globs: apps/api/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Use Postgres for
Transactional, relational, money-touching data: users, portfolios, orders, trades, positions, audit log, OHLCV.

# Use MongoDB for
Flexible or schemaless documents:
- news articles + embeddings metadata
- earnings call transcripts
- raw provider payloads (bronze layer)
- user strategy definitions (JSON DSL)
- chart layout / notebook configs
- social-sentiment snapshots

# Rules
- Collections are typed via `zod` schemas + `@typegoose/typegoose` or hand-written models.
- Never join across Postgres and Mongo in application code for a hot path — denormalize the key you need.
- Use aggregation pipelines (`$facet`, `$lookup`, `$graphLookup`) instead of multi-round trips.
- Create text indexes for any `search` endpoint; measure with `.explain("executionStats")`.
